# Lean browser transport records

The server derives these codecs from the same records used by the LGX pages.
Context values are transport data, never browser-granted authorization.

## A LeanSubmitContext has:
    a csrf, which is Text.
    a key, which is Text.
    an assignment, which is Text.
    a version, which is Int.
    a profile, which is Text.

## A LeanAcceptedJob has:
    an id, which is Text.

## To leanSubmitBody (context: LeanSubmitContext, source: Text, target: Text) -> Text:
    Let entries be a new Seq of JEntry.
    Push a new JEntry with key "schema" and val (a new JStr with s "macsad-lean-submit/1") to entries.
    Push a new JEntry with key "_csrf" and val (a new JStr with s (context's csrf)) to entries.
    Push a new JEntry with key "key" and val (a new JStr with s (context's key)) to entries.
    Push a new JEntry with key "assignment" and val (a new JStr with s (context's assignment)) to entries.
    Push a new JEntry with key "version" and val (a new JStr with s numText(context's version)) to entries.
    Push a new JEntry with key "profile" and val (a new JStr with s (context's profile)) to entries.
    Push a new JEntry with key "source" and val (a new JStr with s source) to entries.
    Push a new JEntry with key "target" and val (a new JStr with s target) to entries.
    Return jsonSerialize(a new JObj with entries entries).
